    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "> I don't think I have MSVC compiler installed\r\n\r\nHi @ma-sadeghi I know nothing about CUDA + Windows, so I took a quick look at the [Installation Guide](https://docs.nvidia.com/cuda/cuda-installation-guide-microsoft-windows/index.html) and found that MSVC needs to be installed before installing CUDA Toolkit. Looks like you're using a Conda environment, but given that we haven't built Windows packages yet (https://github.com/conda-forge/cupy-feedstock/issues/62), I assume that you already have a CUDA Toolkit installed locally, and then install CuPy by wheel (`pip install cupy-cuda102`) in your Conda environment? But this means you should have MSVC somewhere, or NVCC would not work. I am wondering how to make Python discover where your MSVC is...",
